---
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Engineering Coach, Developer, and CTO";
const description =
  "Aaron Saray coaches engineering managers and developers, builds software that stays simple, and leads through honest communication and education.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="relative -mt-header flex min-h-svh flex-col justify-center">
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
        <p
          class="flex items-center text-[clamp(1.2rem,2.8vw,2.1rem)] leading-tight font-semibold text-ink-dim"
        >
          <span
            class="mr-2 flex w-[calc(0.245*clamp(3.5rem,9.5vw,8rem)-0.5rem)] shrink-0 items-center"
          >
            <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-ink-faint"></span>
            <Icon
              name="chevron-right"
              class="-mr-1.5 -ml-[10px] size-4 shrink-0 text-ink-faint"
              strokeWidth={1.5}
            />
          </span>Hi, I'm
        </p>
        <h1
          class="mt-2 text-[clamp(3.5rem,9.5vw,8rem)] leading-[0.95] font-black tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink-display"
        >
          Aaron Saray
        </h1>
        <p
          class="mt-4 text-[clamp(1.55rem,4vw,3rem)] leading-tight font-bold tracking-[-0.01em] text-ink-dim"
        >
          I make things better.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-8 flex justify-center">
        <a href="#how" class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
          <p class="text-base text-ink-mute sm:text-lg">let me show you how</p>
          <Icon
            name="chevron-down"
            class="size-5 animate-drift-down text-ink-faint motion-reduce:animate-none"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="how" class="border-t border-hairline">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-10 sm:px-8 sm:py-14">
        <div
          class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-4 border-b border-hairline py-12 last:border-b-0 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] md:gap-x-12"
        >
          <h2 class="section-title text-lg sm:text-3xl">As a coach</h2>
          <div class="role-copy">
            <p
              class="font-display text-2xl leading-snug font-semibold text-white"
            >
              Good teams are managed on purpose.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
              I coach engineering managers, and the developers who report to
              them. <a href="/2023/self-reflection-as-a-manager/"
                >&ldquo;We tried that before&rdquo;</a
              > is true, but it's never accurate.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
              Managing well means <a href="/2021/must-embrace-conflict/"
                >embracing conflict instead of smoothing it over</a
              >, <a href="/2020/developer-time-vs-manager-time/"
                >protecting developers' time</a
              >, and <a href="/2026/reinventing-the-wheel-is-how-you-learn/"
                >encouraging people to reinvent the wheel</a
              > when appropriate.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-4 border-b border-hairline py-12 last:border-b-0 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] md:gap-x-12"
        >
          <h2 class="section-title text-lg sm:text-3xl">As a developer</h2>
          <div class="role-copy">
            <p
              class="font-display text-2xl leading-snug font-semibold text-white"
            >
              Boring but beautiful code always wins.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
              The longer I write code, the less of it I want to keep. I <a
                href="/2023/an-argument-for-keeping-your-project-simple/"
                >skip the abstraction until I need it</a
              >, <a href="/2022/deleting-vs-fixing-old-code/"
                >delete dead code on sight</a
              >, and <a href="/2021/its-not-lazy-its-reducing-cognitive-load/"
                >automate work that steals valuable time</a
              >.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
              Tooling matters, too. I <a
                href="/2018/understanding-before-package/"
                >understand the problem</a
              > before I reach for a solution, even when that solution <a
                href="/2026/why-im-not-writing-about-ai-yet/"
                >looks like it could just be AI</a
              >.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-4 border-b border-hairline py-12 last:border-b-0 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] md:gap-x-12"
        >
          <h2 class="section-title text-lg sm:text-3xl">As a CTO</h2>
          <div class="role-copy">
            <p
              class="font-display text-2xl leading-snug font-semibold text-white"
            >
              Translation from business to technical, and back again.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
              I stay current with the technology to know the costs and the
              risks, and then <a href="/2026/the-cto-is-a-communicator-first/"
                >explain them to the people deciding</a
              >. Stakeholders <a
                href="/2011/solving-the-problem-not-the-solution/"
                >bring the problem instead of the solution</a
              >, trusting the tech team for the rest.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
              A smaller team isn't immune. With fewer people, <a
                href="/2021/what-non-it-startup-founders-need-to-know/"
                >you need someone weighing the risk for you</a
              > before you decide.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-hairline">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-24 sm:px-8 sm:py-36">
        <h2
          class="max-w-4xl text-[clamp(2rem,5.5vw,4.5rem)] leading-[1.02] font-black tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink-display"
        >
          I want what's best for your project. Not for me.
        </h2>
        <p
          class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim sm:text-xl"
        >
          Bring me the problem and I'll tell you what you actually need.
          Sometimes it isn't a technical problem at all. And if what you need
          isn't me, I'll say that too.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/contact/"
          class="mt-10 inline-flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold text-ink transition-colors duration-300 hover:text-white sm:text-xl"
        >
          Let's talk
          <Icon name="arrow-right" class="size-5 shrink-0" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
